  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the easy version of the problem. It is worth 252525 points in division 111, and 100100100 points in all other divisions.**\n\nFor an array BBB of length MMM, you are allowed to perform the following operation as many times as required:\n\n\nLet S=∑i=1MBiS = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^M{B_i}S=i=1∑M​Bi​\nPick iii such that 1≤i≤min⁡(M,∣S∣)1 \\leq i \\leq \\min(M,|S|)1≤i≤min(M,∣S∣)\nEither increment or decrement BiB_iBi​ by 111\nDefine f(B)f(B)f(B) to be the minimum number of operations needed to turn every element of BBB to 000, or −1-1−1 if it's impossible to achieve.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN. Output the value f(A)f(A)f(A).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the number of elements of the array AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers — the elements of the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the value f(A)f(A)f(A).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "−109≤Ai≤109-10^9 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
