        "input": "5\n4\n1 0 -1 -1\n3\n3 0 1\n2\n0 0\n5\n-2 0 3 -2 2\n4\n2 -3 -1 2",
        "output": "7\n4\n0\n13\n-1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 222: One sequence of four operations is:\n\nDecrement A1A_1A1​ by 111, to get [2,0,1][2, 0, 1][2,0,1]. The sum is now 333.\nDecrement A3A_3A3​ by 111, to get [2,0,0][2, 0, 0][2,0,0]. The sum is now 222.\nDecrement A1A_1A1​ by 111, to get [1,0,0][1, 0, 0][1,0,0]. The sum is now 111.\nDecrement A1A_1A1​ by 111, to get [0,0,0][0, 0, 0][0,0,0].\n\nTest case 333: The array is already filled with zeros.\nTest case 555: It can be shown that it's impossible to make every element 000."
